all right so if you guys watch my video  from yesterday which broke down  apple's one and a half hour long  developer video  you'll know that apple mentioned gaming  on their apple silicon max  many many times so we know that apple is  obviously making a big push for gaming  this year so in this video i want to  respond  to talos of tech in his viewpoint that  gaming isn't going to change  on apple silicon max and i'll explain  why i think  it's actually the opposite now i watched  taylor's of tech's response to my apple  silicon video  on his twitch live stream and first of  all  i want to say that i respect his stance  and his opinion  and i want to thank him for being humble  and respectful  and by the way go and check out his  channel because he makes some very  awesome videos  his viewpoint is that even though apple  is now finally making their metal  graphics tools available on windows  and even though iphone and ipad games  are coming to the mac  it's still not enough to encourage aaa  game developers  to start bringing actually great games  to the mac  his main point is that the gaming market  on the mac is currently not big enough  to make it worth it for developers  which i actually agree with at least  right now  that's why we don't have very many great  games on the mac  and that's the same reason why rocket  league for the mac was cancelled  so now let me explain my viewpoint on  why i think apple silicon  is gonna revive gaming on the mac it's  obvious that this year  apple is putting a huge focus on gaming  so i'll quickly list all of the main  changes  for the first time ever apple is giving  us full-fledged controller support  for third-party controllers across all  of their platforms  including supporting every single button  even  the rear triggers on the xbox  controllers and  the light bar and the touchpad on the  ps4 controller  the ipad is finally getting keyboard and  mouse gaming support for the first time  ever which includes the ability to lock  the pointer  for full screen games apple silicon macs  are going to be able to run  completely unmodified iphone and ipad  apps and games as is on day one  which is huge and they're already  automatically translating touch-based  controls on an iphone  to act as a mouse pointer click drag and  even zoom  and for more complex games since the  ipad is getting keyboard and mouse  gaming support  apple silicon max will instantly get  that functionality as well  for the games that adopt it or of course  they can use a gaming controller instead  apple also completely revamped their  game center  which now supports cross-platform online  multiplayer gaming across the apple tv  the iphone the ipad and the mac  apple is now allowing the resolution and  ui of landscape  iphone and ipad apps to be automatically  resized  to match the native resolution of macs  so 16x9 for the imac  and 16x10 for the macbook and apple is  completely changing up their swift ui  metal apis and coding so that developers  have to do as little work as possible  to support all of apple's platforms and  they're going to continue working on  this every year  with each wwdc event so basically  apple is setting the groundwork or the  foundation  so that if a game developer decides to  bring their game to the mac  it's going to be easier than ever before  it's gonna have much better controller  input support  and it's gonna take less work to  actually maintain the game  now that's where we reach the problem  which is taylor's of tech's  main point how will this encourage game  developers  to actually start bringing their games  to the mac  well first of all the main goal that  game developers have  is to make money and whether this upsets  all of you guys or not  over the past few years mobile gaming  has been quickly taking over the gaming  market  while pc and console gaming has been  slowly going down  and this trend is expected to continue  so realistically  in the long term if game developers want  to make as much money as possible  they eventually need to bring their  games to mobile devices  and that's why we've recently started to  see aaa game developers  transition to mobile gaming here's a  quick list of some of those games  epic games and fortnite pubg mobile  blizzard's heartstone activision's call  of duty mobile  riot games and league of legends wild  rift apex legends mobile  and blizzard's diablo immortal these are  some of the very first  aaa game developers bringing their games  to mobile  because that's where the money's at in  the future and apple silk and max are  going to be able to run  all of those games now i will agree and  admit that the current  x86 aaa windows games that you currently  love to play on your pc  are not gonna come to the mac unless the  developer decides to port it over  but here's why i think aaa games are  gonna make it to the mac  because apple silicon chips in the  iphone and the ipad have been getting so  powerful in recent years  in fact even supporting ray tracing this  shows us that the apple silicon max are  gonna be  even more powerful and based on the  calculations that i made in a previous  video  apple silicon max have a ton of  potential  so within a couple of years of chip  improvements like tsmc's three nanometer  process coming to apple devices  in 2022 the performance will be so good  that game developers will realize that  they can build  much better games for these chips than  ever before and since the mobile gaming  market  is taking over pc gaming with each  passing year more and more  aaa game developers will start creating  better and better mobile games  which will eventually become the aaa  games of the future  that will run on arm-based max and  arm-based pcs  many years down the road and since those  games for the mac will use the same code  base  as on the ipad the iphone and the apple  tv  the developer doesn't have to optimize  and fix bugs  for the various platforms separately  this was the reason why minecraft for  the apple tv was cancelled  and why rocket league on mac was also  cancelled  the developers had to invest a lot of  extra time and money  into maintaining those games for those  platforms  which they won't have to do in the  future so basically this is how i can  imagine triple a games on apple silicon  max  playing out in the future a game  developer will first create a game with  very high quality graphics for the mac  and then make minor and relatively easy  adjustments  like lowering the graphics quality  presets the resolution  and adjusting the ui for every other  apple platform  like the apple tv the ipad and the  iphone  and that way their game supports all  apple devices  while only having to do the bulk of the  code work  one time for the mac so they're reaching  the maximum amount of the apple gaming  market  so if a game developer ultimately wants  to create a game  for the iphone they can first do their  code work as if  it's for the mac and reach all of  apple's platforms  at once instead of just the iphone which  is definitely worth  the work of adjusting the ui and the  resolution across different platforms  and the beauty of it is that when  there's a bug that needs fixing  or code optimizations that need to be  done the developer only has to do it  once since the main code is shared  across the iphone  the ipad the apple tv and the mac this  alone will make it worth it for  developers to bring their games over to  apple silicon max  and since apple now supports universal  purchase across all of their platforms  you can buy the game just once and have  access to it across all of your apple  devices  so a player can play that game on their  apple tv on the big screen  or on their macbook at a coffee shop or  on their ipad on the couch or on their  iphone  while on the bus and their progress is  automatically saved  across all of the platforms and that  person playing on their mac  will get online multiplayer crossplay  support  so they can game with players using any  apple device platform  depending on the input controller device  that he's using  now of course all of this is not gonna  happen overnight  it may take a few years to see this kind  of gaming  fully implemented but what i can tell  you is that this is definitely going to  begin  when apple silicon max start making it  to the market later this year  and game developers realize that they  can kill  four platforms with one code by building  their game for the mac first  and it'll definitely start to begin when  activision blizzard  and other game studios announce how much  revenue  their new mobile games have already  brought in  like the current call of duty mobile and  future games like diablo immortal  and league of legends wild rift and the  even bigger point is that if these  initial changes to gaming that apple  made to their platforms  at this year's wwdc already make  all of the things that i mentioned in  this video possible  imagine what apple is going to announce  at future wwdc events over the next  couple of years  that'll make it even easier and more  worth it for developers  to bring their games to the mac so based  on all of that  i'm extremely confident that apple  silicon is gonna  improve the gaming situation for the mac  since it'll support where the future  gaming market is currently headed  which is gaming on arm architecture  based chips  and this transition will be sped up  significantly  if over the next couple of years apple  silicon turns out to be much more  powerful than we're expecting  which may in turn cause the next version  of windows  to support both x86 and arm-based chips  and maybe in a couple of years intel  will have no other choice than to start  investing more  into making arm-based chips however i do  want to agree with talos of tech on  one point that the current x86 windows  games  that are available on pcs right now  probably  won't be making it to the mac and for  that 